A pool is made over memory a live pool already covers.
Two pools then claim the same words,
and the pool tree is no longer a partition of the memory it manages.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: process maps a pool: isolation broken

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ int process_install(struct process *proc, unsigned slot,
     if (proc->slots[slot].type != CAP_NONE) {
         return KERR_SLOT_IN_USE;
     }
-    if (pool_overlaps(base, size)) {
+    if (0) {
         return KERR_OVERLAP;
     }
     unsigned installed = 0;
